  "content": {
    "id": "v2-2e5df0-p5-practice-slot-2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "For the polynomial $P(x)=(a^2-9)x^3+(a+3)x^2+5x+b-4$, find $a$ and $b$ given that:\n\nThe degree is 2 and the constant term is 3.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=3,\\ b=7$.",
      "worked": "The degree is 2, so the coefficient of $x^3$ is zero and the coefficient of $x^2$ is not zero.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a^2-9&=0\\\\(a-3)(a+3)&=0\\\\a&=3\\ \\text{or}\\ a=-3\\end{align*}$$\n\nIf $a=-3$, then $a+3=0$ and the degree would be less than 2. So $a=3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}b-4&=3\\\\b&=7\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
